    "### Multi-seed robustness check (new)\n",
    "\n",
    "The single run above is one draw of the training randomness: the new head's initialisation,\n",
    "the batch order and the random crops. With only 6-8 training records for some diagnoses,\n",
    "that randomness alone can decide whether a rare class is learned at all.\n",
    "Here the exact same model, hyperparameters, loss and patient split are retrained with\n",
    "3 seeds, and the test metrics are reported as mean ± std. The patient split is kept fixed,\n",
    "so this measures training variance only; the bootstrap above measures test-sample variance."
   ]
  },
